me":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T07:21:19-07:00","id":1485770,"title":"","content":"I would like the writers put out some interesting materials in regard to the more influential and powerful Lasombra Vampires. Not necessarily the ancient and powerful 4th and 5th Generation Lasombra Vampires. I am more interested in established Elders like Talley or Lucita de Aragorn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478293-is-there-any-clan-characters-that-you-should-get-more-screen-time?p=1478297#post1478297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She\u2019s a very minor character, but I have always been intrigued by Elaine de Calinot - Tremere Inner Council member overseeing Africa. She went missing back in the 1990\u2019s and no mention was made of her since. I thought it would have been cool to have her return in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would definitely be nice to see more written about Elaine the Calinot, as well as the other Inner Counsellors who could be said on 'outskirts' - Thomas Wyncham and Xavier de Cincao. These Tremere Vampires do have an important and interesting responsbility, being the Tremere leaders in regard to exotic (under some considerations) regions, with countries and areas full of potential to explore and understand.<br /> The Tremere do have a history of returning - Malgorzata got an Eternal Struggle depicting her as a Tremere Antitribu, Goratrix is supposedly back in V5, and there has been talk about Meerlinda being alright and fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-04-2022, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T00:13:36-07:00","id":1485964,"title":"","content":"I do wanted to know a bit more of what the hell is going with the Tremere. They seem to be in a &quot;we just heard my home exploded&quot; mode, and we know nothing of what their doing, any new objectives. So Karl Schrek, Goramere (cuz I doubt we will know about Tremelot, dead or alive), Carna.... any would be good. Hell, even Aisling after both Draw Distance games.<br /> <br /> But right... how Theo Bell is doing would be nice, even though it might ruin the teories he kind of he killeed Hardestadt as part of a plan, and not simply &quot;got pissed, hated the guy&quot;. <br /> Lucita too... I don't know what the hell is going on with her. If she went full-on Sabbat, if she is on damage control...<br /> I would also love any Giovanni POV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":